{"title":"2000 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_DDM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by DDM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sides of a triangle with positive area have lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. The sides of a second triangle with positive area have lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. What is the smallest positive number that is <b>not</b> a possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/2/e526fbac5ee18e20a7293e9cb9c317989b31988a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x-y|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" />?  \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/9/ee9de156da4825068ab9204c1cde5d2be13ab676.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 2 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 4 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 6 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 8 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"357\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the triangle inequality, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/0/1e0311f8906ebb04964b68e21b87e66a764e9798.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 4 &gt; 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/c/8ac460617bfc48fea8747c0f19e1eced57ae4a39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &gt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />. Also, by the triangle inequality, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/82016782d5c54de6ae30ae73f8a09471fb25ca65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 + 6 &gt; x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/7/4d752abe1a983608aad8871365ab32784698e4cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />.  Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/5/765139cebebea6041573065cd93d1e29268079c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 &lt; x &lt; 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"88\" height=\"15\" />, and by the same logic <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/0/0e0f05b99d7032138640c381dbd0b089133baceb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 &lt; y &lt; 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"17\" />.  \n</p><p>So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are strictly between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.  The length of this interval, which is also the smallest value which cannot be equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/2/e526fbac5ee18e20a7293e9cb9c317989b31988a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x-y|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" />, is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/4/114228a01e21efe5394aa489ccef5bb000ccd93d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />.  For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/a/3fa177c8e8ad089486fb2682f6b008aaf8b5dbec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\leq d &lt; 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"78\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/d/d8d8e915bbfb589f41d4729261e2cff94d83958d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x-y|=d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"88\" height=\"20\" /> can be achieved by setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/7/0c75cb077801b8a10a0f13b18d3d2bcae55355e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, y) = \\left(6+\\frac{d}{2}, 6-\\frac{d}{2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"192\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p>-Jayeed Mahmud, edited by j314andrews\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_DDM\">Video Solution by DDM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by DDM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/wk6VrBamYVI\">https://youtu.be/wk6VrBamYVI</a>\n</p><p>~piggydude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/203JJbC2Clg\">https://youtu.be/203JJbC2Clg</a>\n</p><p>~Thesmartgreekmathdude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10\" title=\"2000 AMC 10\">2000 AMC 10</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems\" title=\"2000 AMC 10 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Answer_Key\" title=\"2000 AMC 10 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_9\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2000 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_11\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2000 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2000 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2000 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <